# Security

## Environment variables

- Never commit secrets. Use `.env.local` (gitignored). Reference `.env.example` for required keys.
- Sanity tokens (`SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN`, etc.) are server-only — never expose in client bundles.
- `SANITY_REVALIDATE_SECRET` is for webhook revalidation routes — validate on incoming requests.

## Headers (`apps/website/next.config.mjs`)

Security headers are intentional: CSP, HSTS, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`.

**Caution:** `X-Frame-Options: DENY` may block Sanity Presentation iframe in production. If visual editing breaks in prod, adjust frame policy for draft/preview routes only — do not remove headers globally.

## CMS content

- Validate and sanitize user-facing CMS output. Use Portable Text renderer, not `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- Image URLs should come from Sanity CDN (`cdn.sanity.io`), not arbitrary external URLs.

## Dependencies

- Pin critical versions at root when needed (e.g. `next` override in root `package.json`).
- Do not add packages without checking existing workspace deps first.
